# Copy to .env and adjust. `.env` is gitignored and must stay that way.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   docker compose up --build

# --- Ports and binding ----------------------------------------------------
# BIND_HOST defaults to 127.0.0.1 in docker-compose.yml. ReviQ has no
# authentication, so exposing it beyond loopback means anyone who can reach
# the port can read every project and resolve every conflict. Change this
# only for a deployment you have secured some other way.
# BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1
# BACKEND_PORT=8000
# FRONTEND_PORT=3000

# Origin the frontend is served from. The backend accepts cross-origin
# requests only from this origin (plus its 127.0.0.1 equivalent).
# REVIQ_ALLOWED_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# --- Data locations -------------------------------------------------------
# Host directory holding the .bib files to import. Mounted read-only.
# BIB_BASE_DIR=./bib_data

# --- Grey-literature retrieval (multivocal reviews only) ------------------
# Read from the process environment and nowhere else. They are never written
# to the database, never returned by the API and never accepted over HTTP —
# app/retrieval/redact.py scrubs them from stored error strings, and the
# interface deliberately offers no field to type them into. A tool that let a
# key be entered through a browser would also have to store it somewhere.
#
# Without these, a project can still import a grey-literature package a
# co-reviewer produced; it just cannot retrieve anything itself.
#
# SearchAPI.io — issues the search queries. https://www.searchapi.io
# SEARCHAPI_API_KEY=
#
# ScrapingBee — fetches and archives the pages the search returned.
# https://www.scrapingbee.com
# SCRAPINGBEE_API_KEY=
#
# Optional. Only for describing figures found in retrieved documents, which is
# off by default and doubles the image size when enabled.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
